<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Give exact values, or decimals correct to 2 decimal places.</p><p>(a) Find the magnitude of <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} -6 \\ -2 \\ 9 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find the distance between <m>P({2},\,{-5},\,{-3})</m> and <m>Q({1},\,{6},\,{2})</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Pythagoras twice: across the floor, then up, gives <m>|\mathbf{r}| = \sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2}</m>.</p><p>(a) <m>\sqrt{({-6})^2 + ({-2})^2 + ({9})^2} = \sqrt{{121}} = {11}</m>.</p><p>(b) <m>\overrightarrow{PQ} = \mathbf{q} - \mathbf{p} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -1 \\ 11 \\ 5 \end{array}\right)}</m>, so <m>PQ = \sqrt{({-1})^2 + ({11})^2 + ({5})^2} = \sqrt{{147}} = {7 \sqrt{3}}</m> <m>\approx {12.12}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>11</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>7 \sqrt{3}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>